    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.448"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    dct:type "resolution-route/computation" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.8"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Public program catalogs can demonstrate selected features such as self-reproduction in simple systems. They cannot resolve the universal definitional conclusion or show that recognition of life must depend only on terrestrial details." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Enumerate a preregistered set of proposed life criteria and simple-rule systems, formalize each criterion, and measure how often systems satisfy it. A criterion absent from broad simple-system searches would challenge the \"almost any\" assertion, while many positive constructions support it only for listed criteria." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "The universe of proposed features is open-ended.", "Self-organization and complexity have competing definitions.", "Simulation analogues may omit causal and material properties of life." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch12-47--gpt--dataset-1> .
